**Current support.** Alpha emits HTML from root activity and expects a
homepage at the selected project root. A deferred general `$entry` purpose will
keep directory routes and add command-specific no-page rules. The earlier
`$page` proposal is superseded and is not current syntax.

### Directory routes

Routes come from directory position, not from the `@` filename:

[codeblock, $code("text"):
    @page.moth          -> index.html
    about/@module.moth  -> about/index.html
]

The root filename is cosmetic. An ordinary file and `index.moth` have no page
meaning.

### Activity and future entry rules

Today a normal root becomes an HTML entry when it has a non-trivial root body,
a direct const fragment or a runtime fragment. A direct builder slot
contribution is a const fragment, so this still emits a complete document:

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    #[$in title:Welcome]
]

The deferred `$entry` design will make the purpose explicit and let `check`
accept a zero-entry project. HTML `build` and `dev` will then need an entry
somewhere below the selected project root, not necessarily at its root, and
single-file HTML output will need one on its selected root. Until that cutover,
the homepage requirement and activity-based selection still apply.

The builder does not invent a homepage or scan arbitrary `.moth` files.
Generated `_dev/` and `_release/` folders remain output, not source.

